.TH FL-SNIP 1 "November 2026" "fldesktop" "fldesktop"
.SH NAME
fl-snip \- take and mark up screenshots
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfl-snip\fR [\fB\-\-snip\fR|\fB\-\-area\fR|\fB\-\-window\fR|\fB\-\-full\fR|\fB\-\-freeform\fR] [\fB\-\-delay\fR \fIN\fR]
.br
\fBfl-snip\fR \fB\-\-edit\fR \fIFILE\fR
.br
\fBfl-snip\fR \fB\-\-pick\-color\fR|\fB\-\-ruler\fR
.br
\fBfl-snip\fR \fB\-\-record\fR [\fB\-\-audio\fR] [\fB\-\-seconds\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-o\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-window\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A snipping tool. The screen is captured first (with \fBgrim\fR(1)) and shown frozen over all
outputs, where you choose what to keep:
.TP
\fBRectangle\fR
Drag a rectangle. A magnifier shows the pixels under the pointer; the arrow keys move the
rectangle (with Shift, change its size) and Enter takes it.
.TP
\fBFreeform\fR
Draw a shape around a part of the screen; what is outside it is transparent.
.TP
\fBWindow\fR
Click a window (fl-wm tells fl-snip where its windows are).
.TP
\fBFull screen\fR
All outputs.
.PP
R, F, W and S switch between them, Esc or a right click cancels.
.PP
Without options fl-snip opens a small window with New, the mode and a delay (none, 3, 5 or
10 seconds). The snip then opens in the editor: pen, highlighter, line, arrow, rectangle,
ellipse, text, pixelate (to hide something) and crop, in seven colors and three widths, with
undo, an eraser for drawings, and a right-click menu. It copies the snip (Ctrl+C), saves it as
PNG (Ctrl+S, Ctrl+Shift+S), opens it in the image viewer or another program, or prints it.
.PP
The quick modes (\fB\-\-area\fR, \fB\-\-window\fR, \fB\-\-full\fR, \fB\-\-freeform\fR) save
the snip to \fI~/Pictures/Screenshots\fR, copy it to the clipboard and print the file's path;
a notification offers to open, edit or show it. \fB\-\-snip\fR opens the editor instead.
.SH COLOUR PICKER AND RULER
\fB\-\-pick\-color\fR shows the frozen screen with the magnifier and the colour under the
pointer; a click (or Enter) prints the colour as \fI#rrggbb\fR and copies it.
\fB\-\-ruler\fR measures: drag from one point to another to see the width, the height and
the distance in screen pixels; Enter or C prints and copies the measurement, Esc closes.
Both are also in the Snip window's More menu.
.SH SCREEN RECORDING
\fBRecord\fR in the Snip window (Ctrl+R), or \fB\-\-record\fR, records a screen or a
window as a WebM video (VP8, 30 frames a second, the pointer included) to
\fI~/Videos/Screencasts\fR. The screen or window is chosen in the screen sharing dialog
of the ScreenCast portal (\fBxdg-desktop-portal-fl\fR(1) in fldesktop); a small window
shows the time and a Stop button. \fB\-\-audio\fR (More > Record with Sound) records the
desktop's sound too (through PipeWire's PulseAudio server). \fB\-\-seconds\fR \fIN\fR
stops after \fIN\fR seconds, \fB\-o\fR names the file, \fB\-\-no\-window\fR shows no
window and no notification (stop with Ctrl+C), and \fB\-\-record\-node\fR \fIN\fR
records PipeWire node \fIN\fR without asking the portal. The file's path is printed.
Recording needs GStreamer with the PipeWire plugin and the good plugins.
.SH KEYS
In fl-wm: \fBPrint\fR the whole screen, \fBShift+Print\fR a rectangle, \fBSuper+Shift+S\fR
a snip to edit.
.PP
In the editor: P, H, L, A, R, E, T, X, C and D choose the pen, highlighter, line, arrow,
rectangle, ellipse, text, pixelate, crop and eraser; Shift keeps lines straight; Ctrl+Z and
Ctrl+Shift+Z undo and redo; Ctrl+wheel, Ctrl++ and Ctrl+\- zoom.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.config/fldesktop/snip.ini\fR
Settings: copy to the clipboard, save to Pictures/Screenshots, include the pointer,
notifications, the last mode and delay.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgrim\fR(1), \fBwl-copy\fR(1), \fBfl-wm\fR(1), \fBfl-view\fR(1)
